WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:07.060
Let's go next to I think I'm pronouncing it
correctly, is it Alida or Alida?

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.520
Yes, it's Alida.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:10.520
How are you Alida?

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:11.520
I'm good.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:12.740
I can't believe I'm talking to you.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.900
I watch you every day.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:15.900
Thank you.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:22.590
My question to you is in regards to the voter
suppression bill in Georgia.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:27.119
Yes, of course, there's been something like
two hundred and fifty three other legislations

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:29.610
going to all 50 states.

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:30.610
Yep.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:33.270
Is there something?

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:38.390
If they don't get it resolved, is there something
that Joe Biden, Joe Biden can do to override

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:39.929
these voter suppression laws?

00:00:39.929 --> 00:00:46.139
I don't know that there's anything Biden can
do, but there is much that the House and Senate

00:00:46.139 --> 00:00:47.139
can do.

00:00:47.139 --> 00:00:53.460
And there is currently a bill that would enshrine
certain voter enfranchisement, voting rights

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:54.460
protections.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:57.499
It's unclear whether that's going to pass.

00:00:57.499 --> 00:01:02.459
I think that this is this is not something
Biden can do directly, but it's certainly

00:01:02.459 --> 00:01:08.180
something the House and Senate can do in a
way that would create a framework that all

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:14.439
states have to meet certain guidelines and
states wouldn't be able to go beyond or ignore

00:01:14.439 --> 00:01:16.240
some of these federal election guidelines.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.280
So that would be that's the path forward,
I think.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:23.430
OK, in order to do that, they would have to
get rid of the filibuster.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:26.439
You think that's a good question?

00:01:26.439 --> 00:01:30.240
I mean, listen, I think I don't know the answer.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:34.509
I, I would like to think there's a way to
get it through the Senate without blowing

00:01:34.509 --> 00:01:35.509
up the filibuster.

00:01:35.509 --> 00:01:37.840
But, yeah, I mean, you're definitely on to
something.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:41.040
It's conceivable that the filibuster would
need to be done away with to pass that.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.969
Yeah, that that's that's quite a possibility.

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:47.460
OK, well, thank you so much, David.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:48.469
My pleasure.

00:01:48.469 --> 00:01:49.890
Great to speak to you.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:53.030
It's good to speak to you to have a good day.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:54.030
You, too, Alida.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.549
Perfect phone call, I would say.

